========================================================================================================
 (2) UNIFORM ARC-COUNT UNION FLOOR + cutoffs:  meas >= meas(L_B)(1-r/7) - (N_B/7) Σ 1/w_j
========================================================================================================
  Per-speed lemma (periodicity repairs the union bound):  meas(L_B ∩ D_w) <= meas(L_B)/7 + N_B/(7w).
  PROOF: D_w = w teeth of width 1/(7w), 1/w-periodic; an arc I meets <= |I|w+1 teeth, each
  contributing <= 1/(7w) => danger in I <= |I|/7 + 1/(7w); sum over the N_B arcs. QED (elementary).
  => cutoff W*(r,m): smallest W with min_m*(1-r/7) - (N/7)(r/W) >= 1/36 for ALL outliers >= W:
    r=1: base min_m=0.056487 (m=10, N=12)  union margin=+0.020640  W*(argmin)=    83.1   UNIFORM W*max=    112.3   #bases with margin<=0: 0
    r=2: base min_m=0.092456 (m=9, N=14)  union margin=+0.038262  W*(argmin)=   104.5   UNIFORM W*max=    181.0   #bases with margin<=0: 0
    r=3: base min_m=0.163920 (m=8, N=18)  union margin=+0.065891  W*(argmin)=   117.1   UNIFORM W*max=    290.0   #bases with margin<=0: 0
    r=4: base min_m=0.217491 (m=7, N=18)  union margin=+0.065433  W*(argmin)=   157.2   UNIFORM W*max=    513.1   #bases with margin<=0: 0

  numeric check of  meas(L_B ∩ D_w) <= meas(L_B)/7 + N_B/(7w)  (worst ratio should be <= 1):
